15. FUNCTIONAL TESTING

Verify all the following cases.

TEST 1:
Lender in Ethiopia creates a physical listing in Ethiopia.

Expected: Successful publication.

TEST 2:
Borrower in Ethiopia attempts to borrow the Ethiopian physical listing.

Expected: Eligible.

TEST 3:
Borrower in Kenya attempts to borrow the Ethiopian physical listing.

Expected: Rejected at frontend and backend.

TEST 4:
Borrower in Kenya accesses a digital listing owned by someone in Ethiopia.

Expected: Digital borrowing remains available under existing rules.

TEST 5:
Lender creates a physical listing with no country.

Expected: Validation error.

TEST 6:
Lender tries to list a physical item in another country while their profile country remains unchanged.

Expected: Listing publication blocked.

TEST 7:
A user tries to retrieve another user's private phone number.

Expected: Unauthorized.

TEST 8:
A user who is not part of a booking tries to retrieve its pickup address.

Expected: Unauthorized.

TEST 9:
A booking is accepted and both parties have authorized contact sharing.

Expected: Appropriate contact information becomes available to the booking participants.

TEST 10:
A user attempts to change their country while they have an active physical booking.

Expected: Existing booking country snapshots and agreements remain intact, and any restricted change follows the defined lifecycle rules.

TEST 11:
An older physical listing has no location information.

Expected: Request its owner to complete the required location fields before making it eligible for new bookings.

TEST 12:
A lender publishes a public business pickup location.

Expected: The explicitly approved public address is visible.

TEST 13:
A lender selects a private residential pickup address.

Expected: Public users see only the approved approximate location; exact details remain protected.

TEST 14:
Phone number uses a country calling code different from the user's profile country.

Expected: Correct number validation and formatting without changing the user's profile country.

